      "content": "It seems the message cut off again. You were starting to explain how the transition from high disorder to a structured state works for these two systems. Could you please complete that thought?\n\nAdditionally, I want to dig a bit deeper into the \"chaos\" aspect I mentioned. In archival science, we often deal with \"noise\" or unexpected, irregular items that don't seem to fit any standard category initially. In your professional opinion, which system is better at containing that sense of disorder or \"messiness\" during the initial cataloging phase without losing the integrity of the collection's overarching structure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
